ar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:21:24-08:00","id":1030038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030031#post1030031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Hunter would do well as Supernatural (early monster-of-the-week episodes) or Buffy.<br /> Geist: Dead Like Me?<br /> Mummy: Maybe something like the Sopranos?<br /> Beast: Dexter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you Vent0. Now I need to completely binge Dexter with a new frame of referene","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5118-perverseness","name":"Perverseness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:17:02-08:00","id":1030148,"title":"","content":"Mummy as The Sopranos? Really? How do you make that connection? <br /> <br /> Dead Like Me... sigh... so much potential. Wasted. <br /> <br /> Also, Dexter as Beast?<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, are there any more fiction novels being written by Onyx Path (hello, A Hunger Like Fire)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:30:49-08:00","id":1030155,"title":"","content":"I still think an American Horror Story type show where each season was its own self-contained story would work well for Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:17:22-08:00","id":1030171,"title":"","content":"I could go for a dark supernatural sitcom, really. Just a regular guy who loudly and comically ignores the supernatural shit around him. He's not the subject of some supernatural conspiracy, or being pulled in opposite directions by supernatural factions, or anything. He's just some loser who randomly and inexplicably bumps into weird shit and refuses to acknowledge it. A running gag is made of him randomly picking up minor templates and refusing to acknowledge them, even as he casually uses the attendant powers for apallingly mundane stuff (sending his Spirit Pack to fetch the morning paper, for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:18:04-08:00","id":1030172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030148#post1030148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy as The Sopranos? Really? How do you make that connection?</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of Mob conflict and drama, it's cult conflict and drama. I mean, it seems like mummy cults would well lend themselves to organized crime. And mummies lend themselves well to conflicted protagonists (in the media focus sense). Instead of family vs business life, it is attempts to regain Memory/humanity vs duty to the Judges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030148#post1030148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead Like Me... sigh... so much potential. Wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030148#post1030148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Dexter as Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily the Serial Killer aspect, as much as &quot;Protagonist character who struggles to channel dark urges into positive goals&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:21:59-08:00","id":1030175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030171#post1030171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could go for a dark supernatural sitcom, really. Just a regular guy who loudly and comically ignores the supernatural shit around him. He's not the subject of some supernatural conspiracy, or being pulled in opposite directions by supernatural factions, or anything. He's just some loser who randomly and inexplicably bumps into weird shit and refuses to acknowledge it. A running gag is made of him randomly picking up minor templates and refusing to acknowledge them, even as he casually uses the attendant powers for apallingly mundane stuff (sending his Spirit Pack to fetch the morning paper, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great. To viewers, it's painfully obvious what's going on, but the protagonist just writes it off as something normal. It would have to have a Scrubs-like internal monolog, though, to explain the ridiculous justification they come up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:27:33-08:00","id":1030178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030175#post1030175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be great. To viewers, it's painfully obvious what's going on, but the protagonist just writes it off as something normal. It would have to have a Scrubs-like internal monolog, though, to explain the ridiculous justification they come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I never did find Scruffy's owner. Must have been some kind of professional animal trainer, though. I've never seen a dog that could separate out the business section before.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:37:35-08:00","id":1030188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030155#post1030155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think an American Horror Story type show where each season was its own self-contained story would work well for Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only challenge I could foresee in an anthology style series is the amount of world building that would have to go into a series involving one of the major game lines. In a dedicated series you could parse most of that out over the first season and then just go from there, but in an anthology series you'd do all that and then immediately start over with something else which would then have to devote time to doing its own world building before giving way to the next thing, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:40:45-08:00","id":1030190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030188#post1030188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only challenge I could foresee in an anthology style series is the amount of world building that would have to go into a series involving one of the major game lines. In a dedicated series you could parse most of that out over the first season and then just go from there, but in an anthology series you'd do all that and then immediately start over with something else which would then have to devote time to doing its own world building before giving way to the next thing, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the answer to that might be leveraging existing material, if not characters or plot, from season to season. Like, establish &quot;weird stuff&quot; season A, but introduce &quot;ghosts&quot; which you focus on in season B, which introduces &quot;spirits&quot; for season C...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:37:04-08:00","id":1030226,"title":"","content":"... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QS_20JPaEnA\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Magicians</i></a> as a Mage inspiration, maybe? :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:12:00-08:00","id":1030270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ROMzombie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030226#post1030226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QS_20JPaEnA\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Magicians</i></a> as a Mage inspiration, maybe? :-D</div> </div> </div> </div>Please god no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T15:31:08-08:00","id":1030279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ROMzombie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030226#post1030226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QS_20JPaEnA\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Magicians</i></a> as a Mage inspiration, maybe? :-D</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030270#post1030270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please god no.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why no? I find <b>Magicians</b> as rather good 'teen Mysterium shool drama' that slowly sinks in to full blown, very dark <b>Changeling</b> crossover. I do not know books, but from what I have heard it's TV series is much more 'edgy'. And I can agree on that seeing 1st season - We have Obsessions driving character, implications on Wise using of power and many beutifull 'oh shit, what we have done' moments. In spirit of 2E <b>Mage</b> we also have storyline about Nameless Order in NYC doing really <i>shady</i> stuff. Really, it's almost like creators read <b>DaveB'</b>s notes on Mage 2E Open Development and try to make TV series out of it, with large twist of <b>Changeling</b> Arcadia madness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:31:45-08:00","id":1030426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv#post1029766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tone could be a challenge of sorts. Certain lines make easy comparisons for TV, but others.... at a basic level, I figure:<br /> <br /> Requiem: Game of Thrones political intrigue<br /> Forsaken: Sons of Anarchy<br /> Awakening: some kind of detective show? Really unsure.<br /> Promethean: ?<br /> Changeling: court intrigue as well? Unsure.<br /> Hunter: procedural?<br /> Geist: no idea, but all over it.<br /> Demon: Person of Interest<br /> Mummy: ?<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, this will never happen; the cost alone to have it not look like amateur hour would be eye watering. But a guy can dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening works really well for an Occult Investigation show, that starts procedural but slowly builds its own overarching mythos. The images in my head of the initial pov character is a newly Awakened Acanthus, and there's a more senior Mastigos bad-ass who leads the Cabal that's training her.<br /> <br /> Actually I may want to switch their genders, just so you can have &quot;Actually I'm the warlock, and he's the witch&quot;...<br /> <br /> <br /> Mummy would definitely need to be structured with shorter seasons, but could be really cool and it deals with amnesia, mysteries, and gradual backstory reveals that the characters themselves learn and interact with through flashbacks that are borderline time-travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-12-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T21:48:46-08:00","id":1030432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030279#post1030279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why no? I find <b>Magicians</b> as rather good 'teen Mysterium shool drama' that slowly sinks in to full blown, very dark <b>Changeling</b> crossover. I do not know books, but from what I have heard it's TV series is much more 'edgy'. And I can agree on that seeing 1st season - We have Obsessions driving character, implications on Wise using of power and many beutifull 'oh shit, what we have done' moments. In spirit of 2E <b>Mage</b> we also have storyline about Nameless Order in NYC doing really <i>shady</i> stuff. Really, it's almost like creators read <b>DaveB'</b>s notes on Mage 2E Open Development and try to make TV series out of it, with large twist of <b>Changeling</b> Arcadia madness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Short version (without turning this into a full on review and derailing the thread). <br /> There are good parts in it, but they're weighed down by an equal if not greater number of perplexingly terrible writing choices and the fact that nearly all the main characters are loathsome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T22:45:38-08:00","id":1030446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030432#post1030432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short version (without turning this into a full on review and derailing the thread).<br /> There are good parts in it, but they're weighed down by an equal if not greater number of perplexingly terrible writing choices and the fact that nearly all the main characters are loathsome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, plenty of room for somebody else to do it better, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T08:31:51-08:00","id":1030600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030426#post1030426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy would definitely need to be structured with shorter seasons, but could be really cool and it deals with amnesia, mysteries, and gradual backstory reveals that the characters themselves learn and interact with through flashbacks that are borderline time-travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arrow-like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T09:19:39-08:00","id":1030616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030600#post1030600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Arrow-like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Way less episodically structured than that, and the characters themselves don't remember until the reveals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T13:49:37-08:00","id":1030767,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking the sounds of some of these suggestions. I've even gone away and thrown my Storymatic at some of these lines.<br /> <br /> SUCH fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T14:32:14-08:00","id":1030797,"title":"","content":"Requiem would definitely be a <i>\u200bGame of Thrones</i>-style show, focusing on a lot of political intrigue. Actually, the set-up of <i>\u200bGame of Thrones </i>would work quite well for a Requiem show: a sudden power vacuum in a domain lights of fuse of political intrigue that explodes into large-scale conflict as everybody ignores a mounting existential threat. Shocking deaths would be par for the course, and vampire feeding methods being what they are, that could be the excuse for the <i>Game of Thrones</i>-style fan service if HBO picks up the show. <br /> <br /> I know people want to say <i>Sons of Anarchy </i>as the Forsaken inspiration, but I think it's more a hybrid of <i>SoA </i>and <i>Blue Bloods, </i>since a big part of Forsaken is the whole &quot;policing the spirits&quot; things, and <i>SoA </i>doesn't fully capture that angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T18:03:04-08:00","id":1030896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030797#post1030797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know people want to say <i>Sons of Anarchy </i>as the Forsaken inspiration, but I think it's more a hybrid of <i>SoA </i>and <i>Blue Bloods, </i>since a big part of Forsaken is the whole &quot;policing the spirits&quot; things, and <i>SoA </i>doesn't fully capture that angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken 2E is a lot less about &quot;policing the spirits&quot; now... unless that happens to be your Pack or Tribe's thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T21:10:20-08:00","id":1030998,"title":"","content":"Given paradox's current plans, I really think the best way to introduce the CofD after they introduce the WoD is with what someone here called Crisis on infinite worlds of darkness, a miniseries involving a threat to both worlds that rips open a rift between the two universes as it tries to smash them into each other and destroy them. Have it be a mini series that introduces the CofD to the fans of the already existing WoD tv or netflix series. Feature lots of fighting (Beckett VS the Unholy needs to happen, as does an epic mexican standoff between TFV, the SAD, VASCU, the Malleus Maleficarum and the Society of Leopold) and romancing (maybe have an iconic Ivory Claw lady try to seduce king <b>Albrecht</b>) between the iconic characters of both worlds.<br /> <br /> The finale, of course, has the threat dealt with in a way that suppresses the memories of it for all involved, but leaves open the possibly of them remembering during the inevitable sequal miniseries","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:29:39-08:00","id":1031207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1030998#post1030998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given paradox's current plans, I really think the best way to introduce the CofD after they introduce the WoD is with what someone here called Crisis on infinite worlds of darkness, a miniseries involving a threat to both worlds that rips open a rift between the two universes as it tries to smash them into each other and destroy them. Have it be a mini series that introduces the CofD to the fans of the already existing WoD tv or netflix series. Feature lots of fighting (Beckett VS the Unholy needs to happen, as does an epic mexican standoff between TFV, the SAD, VASCU, the Malleus Maleficarum and the Society of Leopold) and romancing (maybe have an iconic Ivory Claw lady try to seduce king <b>Albrecht</b>) between the iconic characters of both worlds.<br /> <br /> The finale, of course, has the threat dealt with in a way that suppresses the memories of it for all involved, but leaves open the possibly of them remembering during the inevitable sequal miniseries</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the person who coined that was me, but it was in the context of saying it would be a terrible idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:36:38-08:00","id":1031215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1029766-cofd-tv?p=1031207#post1031207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the person who coined that was me, but it was in the context of saying it would be a terrible idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, for the basis of a campaign, it could be fun, but yeah, for any sort of media, it's kind of an awful idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:27:25-08:00","id":1031234,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. But maybe there is a way to do a crossover that isn't terrible","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:52:45-08:00","id":1031245,"title":"","content":"So I've actually thought for a while about how CofD could translate into a TV show. I think that each game line should have its own series, a lot like the Defenders. Each series however focuses on a group of characters that interact with each other a la Game of Thrones: power struggles, schemes, violence, and friendships/allegiances/love affairs. The first series/season would be focused on Requiem, and the different clans/covenants fighting for control of a city. Depending on how good the series is, it may be greenlit for a second season. However, in every series/gameline, there is a character or group of characters that cross over representing another game line, similar to how Claire Temple and Turk cross over in the various Marvel Defenders shows. They could be mages and werewolves working with the Vampires, which leads into their own series. I think that would be pretty badass. Also, because it's shared universe, events from one show could have some kind of affect on other shows. Plus, you would have to have a human character or two caught in the cross-fire, so that the viewer could relate to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}